I collapsed the two early returns into a single result variable, so the hot path is one comparison and the profile-type load can be emitted as a conditional move instead of a second branch.

```cpp
FIT_UINT8 Field::GetType() const
{
    FIT_UINT8 result = type;
    if ( result == FIT_UINT8_INVALID )
    {
        const auto p = profile;
        if ( (p != NULL) && (profileIndex < p->numFields) )
            result = p->fields[profileIndex].type;
    }
    return result;
}
```